3. HOW EACH DIMENSIONAL FIGURE SCALES WITH G (sympy, from wall.py's formulas)
      d ln F / d ln G = -1     rho ceiling (2.658e-4 kg/m^3)
      d ln F / d ln G = 1/3    R_min at N=1 (965 m) and N=0.1 (4.48 km)
      d ln F / d ln G = 1/2    e-foldings of a fixed (M,R) ship
      d ln F / d ln G = 0      R at ceiling, fixed x (1034 AU, 2850 AU)
      d ln F / d ln G = -1     M at ceiling in kg
      d ln F / d ln G = 0      M at ceiling in Msun, M_sun = GM_sun/G (consistent)
      d ln F / d ln G = -1     M at ceiling in Msun, M_sun a fixed kg number (wall.py)
      d ln F / d ln G = 1      x of the 1000 t, 4478 m ship (3.3e-25)
      d ln F / d ln G = 0      wall areal density, x->0 (3.97 g/m^2)
      d ln F / d ln G = 1      wall tension, x->0 (1.5e-11 N/m)
      d ln F / d ln G = 0      marginal shortfall / adiabatic margin (1.8e14, 2.2e14)
  rho ceiling ~ 1/G                                                  ok   
  R_min ~ G^(1/3)                                                    ok   
  R at ceiling is G-INDEPENDENT                                      ok   
  M in Msun is G-INDEPENDENT when M_sun = GM_sun/G                   ok   
  areal density at fixed (M,R) is G-INDEPENDENT (the mass closes)    ok   
  the 1.8e14 / 2.2e14 inversion figures carry no G                   ok   

